    Fix DistSQL SET DIST VARIABLE for boolean properties with 1/0 (#25389) (#40544)
    
    Boolean properties previously fell back to Boolean.valueOf(value), so values
    such as 1 or 0 were silently converted to false instead of being honored or
    rejected. Parse them explicitly as TRUE/FALSE/1/0 case-insensitively and reject
    any other value with InvalidVariableValueException. Non-boolean properties are
    untouched.
    
    Add unit tests for the enabled/disabled numeric values and for invalid values,
    and document the accepted boolean literals in EN/CN user manual.

